WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:02.602
Later, Steven and I headed into the mountains

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:06.302
to Bongeunsa, a Buddhist meditation temple

00:00:06.302 --> 00:00:08.682
founded more than a thousand years ago.

00:00:08.682 --> 00:00:10.162
We were fortunate enough to talk

00:00:10.162 --> 00:00:11.781
to one of the eight Buddhist monks

00:00:11.781 --> 00:00:13.162
who live at the compound,

00:00:13.162 --> 00:00:15.211
and the results were enlightening.

00:00:18.042 --> 00:00:22.041
(man speaks in Korean)
His name is Haneul.

00:00:22.041 --> 00:00:23.361
His name is Haneul.

00:00:23.361 --> 00:00:25.101
You must be very at peace.

00:00:25.101 --> 00:00:26.821
He must be very at peace in his spirit

00:00:26.821 --> 00:00:27.781
and his mind.

00:00:27.781 --> 00:00:29.861
(man speaks in Korean)

00:00:29.861 --> 00:00:31.341
What is he saying?
He's saying,

00:00:31.341 --> 00:00:33.001
"You need to look inside yourself

00:00:33.001 --> 00:00:35.421
"to fix your problems."
(laughter)

00:00:35.421 --> 00:00:36.961
Which, I mean...

00:00:36.961 --> 00:00:38.941
I don't want to look in there, I already know.

00:00:38.941 --> 00:00:40.541
It's such a peaceful place,

00:00:40.541 --> 00:00:42.921
but the wind chimes are making me crazy.

00:00:42.921 --> 00:00:45.641
It's like, peace and then grrr!

00:00:45.641 --> 00:00:47.640
(laughter)
Makes me crazy!

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.071
(man speaks Korean)

00:00:59.751 --> 00:01:03.251
This guy could (mumbles) talking for (mumbles) straight.

00:01:06.401 --> 00:01:09.640
I think when you live here and you're around all these

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.740
very peaceful monks,

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.960
you must have this urge to speak.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.980
It's these wind chimes.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:17.960
They make me crazy in my head.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.015
Crazy! The wind chimes!
(laughter)

00:01:20.015 --> 00:01:22.934
(speaks Korean)
(laughter)

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:25.424
My mind, it's just, like, crazy!

00:01:26.435 --> 00:01:30.053
(man speaks Korean)

00:01:30.053 --> 00:01:31.533
He knows that you're on T.V.

00:01:31.533 --> 00:01:33.153
You know that I'm on T.V.?

00:01:33.153 --> 00:01:34.413
You have television?

00:01:34.413 --> 00:01:36.863
(laughter)

00:01:37.873 --> 00:01:40.053
I really thought we were the first people

00:01:40.053 --> 00:01:42.549
to come up here in a thousand years.

00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:44.250
(Man speaks Korean)

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:45.509
You have an iPhone?

00:01:45.509 --> 00:01:48.270
(man speaks Korean)
What'd he say?

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.170
He says he has both.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:49.910
What does he have?

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:51.149
He has Samsung and an iPhone.

00:01:51.149 --> 00:01:52.650
You have Samsung and an iPhone?

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:55.229
I don't even have that!

00:01:55.229 --> 00:01:58.479
(traditional Korean music)

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.729
(man speaks Korean)

00:02:16.729 --> 00:02:18.519
Because the chimes aren't enough, you know.

00:02:21.229 --> 00:02:22.737
What'd I do wrong?

00:02:24.347 --> 00:02:25.495
Oh, I see.

00:02:30.564 --> 00:02:32.075
You're laughing at me.
(laughter)

00:02:33.945 --> 00:02:34.782
Let me try one more time.

00:02:34.782 --> 00:02:35.843
I think I've got it.

00:02:35.843 --> 00:02:39.133
I got it, I got it.
(laughter)

00:02:41.081 --> 00:02:43.492
Very different, little difference.

00:02:48.182 --> 00:02:50.782
(man speaks Korean)

00:02:50.782 --> 00:02:52.392
What did I do wrong?

00:03:00.122 --> 00:03:01.632
(man and Steven speaking Korean)

00:03:01.632 --> 00:03:03.160
You two are having a big old laugh.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.050
(laughter)

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:12.380
(applause and cheering)

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:21.889
Oh.
(laughter)

00:03:23.758 --> 00:03:24.938
What are you going to do with this guy?

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.938
I don't know.
(laughter)

00:03:26.938 --> 00:03:27.895
Good luck.

00:03:27.895 --> 00:03:29.816
It took us years to master this.

00:03:29.816 --> 00:03:31.365
(laughter)

00:03:40.536 --> 00:03:43.015
(traditional Korean music)

00:03:43.015 --> 00:03:45.124
Yeah, yeah, yeah, OK.

00:03:46.584 --> 00:03:48.012
I know how to shovel!

00:03:49.512 --> 00:03:50.912
I'm from Boston!

00:03:50.912 --> 00:03:53.032
We have snow!

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:55.451
(Man speaking Korean)

00:03:55.451 --> 00:03:58.341
(cell phone ringing)
(laughter)

00:04:00.189 --> 00:04:03.138
(laughter and applause)

00:04:08.689 --> 00:04:11.939
(laughter and applause)

00:04:14.785 --> 00:04:18.235
(laughter and applause)

